{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerUnitCircle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerUnitCircle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerUnitCircle.lean#L55-L67","doc":"The Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm on the unit circle:\n`D(e^{iθ}) = Cl_2 θ`, where `Cl_2` is the Clausen function\n(`ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean`).\n\n**2026-11-15 (owner decision, issue #7942):** this was a\n`noncomputable opaque` with no body, which made every statement\nabout its values independent of Lean.  It now carries its documented\nbody `Cl_2 θ`.  Consequence: the old `BringZeroModeBlochClass` field\n(*some* real angle) became an intermediate-value fact\n(`BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean`), so the field was restated over\nalgebraic Bloch–Wigner combinations; it has no instance.  The root-of-unity (transcendence-obstructed)\nversion is the separate class `BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}